# The projection editor's arrangement rows (Scenograph editor plan, E5): one
# row per declared option, placeholders that say what a blank row means, a
# refusal in the compiler's words, and rows rebuilt when the arrangement
# changes. The practice projection starts on Grid with three items.
assert title GRAPHSHELL H3 READY
act load-practice-projection
settle 2
dom click [data-projection-panel="arrangement"]
settle 2
assert attr #gs-projection-option-cell_width placeholder 164 (the largest item's width)
assert attr #gs-projection-option-columns placeholder 2 (the side of the square that holds every item)
type #gs-projection-option-columns 0
settle 2
assert dom #gs-projection-option-columns-refusal needs a positive whole number
assert attr #gs-projection-option-columns aria-invalid true
assert snap projection-executable == false
type #gs-projection-option-columns 3
settle 2
assert attr #gs-projection-option-columns aria-invalid false
assert snap projection-executable == true
type #gs-projection-arrangement-kind spiral
settle 2
assert dom #gs-projection-arrangement-options Curve
select #gs-projection-option-curve linear
settle 2
assert snap projection-executable == true
type #gs-projection-arrangement-kind nothing.like.it
settle 2
assert dom #gs-projection-arrangement-options names no built-in arrangement or registered solver
capture projection_options
wait
log projection editor arrangement rows proof complete
